  <!-- ===================== ABOUT ===================== -->
  <section id="about">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <div class="rule"></div>
        <h2>About</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>I'm a product manager based in Mumbai with nine-plus years across fintech, media-tech and insurance. Most of my work sits where a large consumer business meets a digital one — mobile apps, payments rails, internet banking platforms — figuring out what to build, writing the BRD that gets engineering and business aligned, and staying with a feature through sprint planning to the release that actually moves a number.</p>
        <p>I started in SEO and digital marketing in Pune and Dubai, then spent two years at Future Generali managing online aggregator accounts and digital channels. From there I moved into banking: business loans at YES BANK, where I helped scale monthly disbursals and shipped an instant-loan product that won a CEO Award, then internet banking and UPI at Axis Bank, rebuilding the UPI module end to end for a national mandate.</p>
        <p>Since November 2022 I've been at Tata Play, owning core modules of the mobile app — self-care, recharge, pack management — and leading features like UPI Mandate Auto Pay, CVV-less recharge and the Amazon Prime Video and Binge integrations. Designing for a base that spans metros and small towns, and smartphone-first users alongside long-time cable customers, is the most interesting part of the job.</p>
        <p>What I care about: a BRD clear enough that engineering doesn't have to guess, a sprint process the team actually trusts, and product decisions that show up in a revenue line, not just a roadmap slide.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ===================== EXPERIENCE ===================== -->
  <section id="experience" class="alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <div class="rule"></div>
        <h2>Experience</h2>
        <p>Nine years across entertainment, banking, insurance and digital marketing.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="timeline">

        <article class="role">
          <div class="role-card">
            <h3>Product Manager — Mobile App &amp; Website</h3>
            <div class="company">Tata Play Ltd</div>
            <div class="meta">November 2022 – Present &nbsp;|&nbsp; Mumbai</div>
            <ul>
              <li>Own critical modules of the Tata Play mobile app, including Native Self-Care, Recharge and Manage Packs, directly tied to revenue generation.</li>
              <li>Led end-to-end delivery of Native Recharge, CVV-less Recharge, UPI Mandate (Auto Pay), Amazon Prime Video integration, Manage Pack Revamp, NPS improvements, the Recharge Widget and Sports Event Page enhancements.</li>
              <li>Drove OTT revenue growth by spearheading the Binge app integration and upsell initiatives.</li>
              <li>Managed website deliverables including Manage Pack Revamp, Recharge 2.0 and Binge Delink, coordinating across Enterprise, Finance and Marketing teams.</li>
              <li>Built a common logic platform to keep customer-facing functionality consistent across app and website.</li>
              <li>Implemented Agile Story Points across delivery teams and created a standardised BRD format now used by Business, IT and Tech.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="role">
          <div class="role-card">
            <h3>Product Manager — Internet Banking &amp; UPI</h3>
            <div class="company">Axis Bank Ltd.</div>
            <div class="meta">October 2020 – November 2022 &nbsp;|&nbsp; Mumbai</div>
            <ul>
              <li>Led a complete UPI module revamp on the Axis Mobile App, including UPI Number functionality under an NPCI mandate for all PSP apps, and UPI Mandate (Auto Pay).</li>
              <li>Managed the Internet Banking revamp, delivering FD/RD, Outward Remittance, Credit Card and Quick Transfer modules.</li>
              <li>Ran multi-channel migration campaigns (SMS, email, push) to drive adoption of the new IB platform.</li>
              <li>Implemented Agile weekly sprint execution to speed up delivery, and built product decks used by internal and external stakeholders.</li>
              <li>Trained the Customer Service team on new platform features on a regular cadence.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="role">
          <div class="role-card">
            <h3>Product Manager — Business Loans</h3>
            <div class="company">Yes Bank Ltd.</div>
            <div class="meta">July 2019 – October 2020 &nbsp;|&nbsp; Mumbai</div>
            <ul>
              <li>Scaled Business Loan monthly disbursals from INR 35–40 Cr to INR 50 Cr through coordination with the Sales team.</li>
              <li>Delivered 'Business Loan In Seconds' (BLIS), an instant loan disbursal product that made Yes Bank only the second bank in India to launch the capability — recognised with a CEO Award.</li>
              <li>Integrated new digital lending partners and tracked Sales Force productivity.</li>
              <li>Ran digital marketing campaigns (voice blast, SMS, email) and handled channel payout validation and product mix optimisation.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="role">
          <div class="role-card">
            <h3>Deputy Manager — Marketing</h3>
            <div class="company">Future Generali India Life Insurance</div>
            <div class="meta">June 2017 – July 2019 &nbsp;|&nbsp; Mumbai</div>
            <ul>
              <li>Managed key online aggregator accounts — Policybazaar, Coverfox, PolicyX, My Money Mantra — on a daily basis.</li>
              <li>Designed and ran R&amp;R programs for channel partners and managed vendor relationships and digital integration.</li>
              <li>Grew LinkedIn and Glassdoor followers by 200% in three months through a new social media strategy.</li>
              <li>Implemented the Simplify360 ORM tool end to end for the organisation and managed the company intranet and newsletter.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="role">
          <div class="role-card">
            <h3>SEO Engineer</h3>
            <div class="company">Softusvista Inc.</div>
            <div class="meta">January 2015 – June 2015 &nbsp;|&nbsp; Pune</div>
            <ul>
              <li>Designed SEO-optimised websites — keyword analysis, content creation, site architecture and meta-tag strategy.</li>
              <li>Ran keyword and competitive analysis using Google Analytics and Google Keyword Planner.</li>
              <li>Built out cpu.specshero.com and sportscars.myautoclub.com.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="role">
          <div class="role-card">
            <h3>Management Trainee</h3>
            <div class="company">Navaida Solutions &amp; Services</div>
            <div class="meta">March 2016 – May 2016 &nbsp;|&nbsp; Dubai</div>
            <ul>
              <li>Acquired 6 new clients and generated 30 qualified leads through digital marketing and social strategy.</li>
              <li>Grew company social media presence by 200%, earning a Pre-Placement Offer for the performance.</li>
              <li>Led competitive research, audience identification and brand benchmarking.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </article>

